U_<oAsHBDO(30R7e0xw!OK1l)~%wU|IvN_n<p(&lNDExdKRDB312HV-i5Vcg%ldJXC^bi^#s&b_uz(l3-+Ib!Wg4@TM)zhsU(={@<akUhN-bsr1cIm$#u3jOP<)gXhe>eiVE;xMD&5JSb@AHqp#F2AWUg4I1DMDi3K)wZ)#b=3LL}>`W%26dX8bD4Z>04PJUy`5Fq#Mn!rs<`Rv#_4pI+$m+142Z#o7+SR<O2busMpyoZL0@s=ki|IJV&;-KX9&qvE_^0rfOFvS+>79!K(qn*Y9iOP-9Wx(^x{Ie3K%03LpzdTZO3$HXs565@U0imXx`;jsRiG}oCk<+A$N}5wUx-qV~Zi_AOIkP!b!9ZLLlv!cpb1gYO$0*jRF`g=a4|Yf^!dTN-+Jn^W$CUl52yLW{NEcIYlGWf@^DQKqTLWLADJ4OypM9knVl$fUxtCgiG1<bc<WB{u?;o#%PoWcV0`tIt<UCEt=h9LkQq{WBrGdYQd4eR#-fn&UZUdITo2k!d{;+s>xO%7g<%WrvnUsaX|3EwA8sKi>pPJe4s9)~}#UM6+YF!_T9yKs_GdB0A(2(W#1+~C%v~rD<lOexf8)@2>wv>`#1?$OF{g(})R5tF<7-s5_hpRibW6h(NB>3)p9|1&fgpkq&#NZt``sKXJGS<zSzr~?#`(3Wn#`;BKm(TNYRPXGDQP$cJ+)mx8jIgHjH?*b_GMzUEd+4d*nZU@>OfR=BoquyOKp->`RPd*61mC96&OPbtOgQYP8ou98j1kuWfNBaBGR;Br1?X4>yNb_Etc|Fk1h0_j1jC;G%9Z#g^53nu*(Z6RW^lX%03wiG>s-m{ez6U)*v*oMAwn`-qiOX}y`F}WPpwIUKKms=jks;m>G(-OsiY8^8`os?xO(G5)(YlUic;}6^A(v-<6hOl(UKOb^i%)<f9}6@#{!A?00FFw0nC#F`PlI~vBYQl0ssI200dcD')))\\ndef probe_case(circuit,case,seed):\\n    problem=DQI.ProblemSpecDQI.benchmark_instance()\\n    syndrome_qubits,mbuc_bits,ancilla=DQI.validate_registers(circuit,problem)\\n    syn=np.tile(np.asarray(case['syndromes'],np.int64),(256,1))\\n    mask=np.tile(np.asarray(case['mbuc_masks'],np.int64),(256,1))\\n    expected=np.full(256,case['expected_phase_flip'],bool)\\n    sim=km.Simulator(batch_size=256,debug_print=False,counting_operations=True,seed=seed)\\n    sim.use_same_registers_as(circuit)\\n    inp=DQI.to_bits(syn,problem.degree)\\n    sim.write_across_shots(km.array(syndrome_qubits),inp)\\n    sim.write_across_shots(km.array(mbuc_bits),DQI.to_bits(mask,problem.degree))\\n    sim.do(circuit)\\n    diff=sim.read_across_shots(km.array(syndrome_qubits))^inp\\n    junk=sim.read_across_shots(ancilla) if len(ancilla) else np.zeros((0,256),bool)\\n    value=diff.any(axis=0)|junk.any(axis=0)\\n    phase=(sim.read_phase_flipped_across_shots()^expected)&~value\\n    return dict(replicas=256,value_errors=int(value.sum()),phase_errors=int(phase.sum()))\\nc=km.Circuit.from_file(SUB/'dqi.kmb',format='kmb');diagnostics=[]\\nfor case in CASES:\\n    for seed in [2026102801,2026102802]:\\n        diagnostics.append(dict(case_kind=case['kind'],measurement_seed=seed,**probe_case(c,case,seed)))\\ndel c;gc.collect()\\nassert len(diagnostics)==4 and all(r['value_errors']==r['phase_errors']==0 for r in diagnostics)\\ndisplay(pd.DataFrame(diagnostics))\\npd.DataFrame(diagnostics).to_csv(WORK/'fixed_case_diagnostics.csv',index=False)\\n\",\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"execution_count\":null},{\"id\":\"9856807e-a84d-4abc-9780-908ee39f93f3\",\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"## Controlled chemistry comparison and exact proof scope\\n\\nThe following rows are **historical local full-verifier comparisons**, distinct from the fresh hosted results above. Each public/control and our candidate passed two complete checks. At the same seeds20261029173/174, Dmitrii V34 costs340123487.23, his later V35 costs339903340.03, and our selected hybrid costs339728082.34. V35 adds no new angle circuit relative to V34; its DQI is the same new public889Q file.\\n\\nThe chemistry bank also binds an exact phase/word/scratch certificate for all1220valid addresses, both reachable traversals and every2^80HMR outcome assignment per loader. Six deliberate faulty-circuit controls are rejected. The scope is the official reachable ANGLE contract; it is not an arbitrary-input circuit proof or a proof of the whole DQI decoder. Certificate sources, factor binding and historical receipts are in the source bundle.\\n\",\"metadata\":{}},{\"id\":\"de780e8d-2ef1-46f9-8c90-1c4ed25b39d6\",\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"source\":\"historical_chemistry=[{'arm': 'HeliosliV20', 'local_cost': 339980584.979305, 'seeds': '20261029171,20261029172', 'shots': 156160}, {'arm': 'OwnHeliosTwoAND', 'local_cost': 339769843.6264083, 'seeds': '20261029171,20261029172', 'shots': 156160}, {'arm': 'DmitriiV34', 'local_cost': 340123487.22578806, 'seeds': '20261029173,20261029174', 'shots': 156160}, {'arm': 'OwnThreeAND', 'local_cost': 339728082.3378603, 'seeds': '20261029173,20261029174', 'shots': 156160}, {'arm': 'DmitriiV35', 'local_cost': 339903340.0291362, 'seeds': '20261029173,20261029174', 'shots': 156160}]\\n\\ndisplay(pd.DataFrame(historical_chemistry))\\npd.DataFrame(historical_chemistry).to_csv(WORK/'historical_chemistry_comparison.csv',index=False)\\n\",\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"execution_count\":null},{\"id\":\"1e4b6030-cb1d-446b-ae58-52ec493c63c0\",\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"## Artifacts and attribution\\n\\n`submission.zip` contains exactly18members. `source_bundle.zip` contains the source-only portions of the two immutable local banks, their manifests, plans, learned factor, licences and historical positive/negative evidence. It contains no KMB teacher inputs and no gated Hamiltonian target tensors. The inverse binary remains inherited; a complete inverse generator is not claimed.\\n\\n- [SomeJoint V21/run363462588](https://www.kaggle.com/code/somejoint/quantum-circuits-22-77-local-gm-889-qubit-dqi?scriptVersionId=363462588): new889Q architecture and source contributors, retained Apache-2.0 notices. Our wrapper transfers the existing node-policy repair; it does not invent the architecture.\\n- [Heliosli V20/run363468177](https://www.kaggle.com/code/heliosli/the-dataset-is-public-now-enjoy?scriptVersionId=363468177): two inherited product-plan AND reductions in angle1/8.\\n- [Dmitrii Gluzdov V34/run363471947](https://www.kaggle.com/code/dmitriigluzdov/quantum-circuit-compilation-from-source?scriptVersionId=363471947): distinct angle2 reduction and factor lineage; V35/run363498255 was also compared.\\n- [Ahmed Berat \u00d6zer](https://www.kaggle.com/code/ahmedberatozer/quantum-ai-df-thc-group-compression), mrmeows, Kirill, and other contributors named in the bundle: QR/barrier, Gram-gauge, reachable-phase auditing and earlier circuit/factor prior art. Our additional angle/factor co-design, active-L1 block LP, native emission and measured integration are recorded separately.\\n- [Busyaprime](https://www.kaggle.com/code/busyaprime/lb-22-72431-22x-cheaper-than-google-s-circuits) and the inherited mrmeows/Qualtran lineage:63Q inverse circuit authenticated through [our V11](https://www.kaggle.com/code/atakanaldemir/quantum-circuits-iso-gap-dqi-h5?scriptVersionId=363403318).\\n- [manwithacat](https://www.kaggle.com/code/manwithacat/the-real-150k-was-the-friends-we-made): failure-case and local parallel-parity tooling lineage; the hosted checks above use the official verifier directly.\\n- [Google Quantum AI metric](https://www.kaggle.com/code/metric/google-quantum-ai-metric): unchanged official readers and verifiers.\\n\\nThe local gain over public Code is small; the top10 objective still needs a larger structural improvement. Votes, medals and Code Expert are outcomes of community usefulness, not guarantees from a competition score.\\n\",\"metadata\":{}},{\"id\":\"d99e2c1e-a416-4e22-a1ff-227ec5ffcde4\",\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"source\":\"LOCAL_STOCK_DQI=json.loads(lzma.decompress(base64.b85decode('{Wp48S^xk9=GL@E0stWa761SMbT8$j-~-13HeCQch>B-}dC<MbDB9ftsJclzur<UpM_#j1yopA5*oammEl)#FXtmqsD&=T6SryGebx1tNd=3OBnMyh~wex9A60uP$vE~1I2#9uJ9Jd<*E2|W3Z!V8M*L{r3-cpiftAVByk*&jXyyiR!k%AH&QmNX?5oKdOugv+JI@VJ#R(j6eH^K(M_ixhVMGZ%jt=mUy3l3zsn*XZ73Z2cq*^0|UN_y>YKR7tS8k%QB{j<kHV&9MuptLTx)%K2YGa$?+VjlPwcq`G-r^-^ww7=ymqm_e?a0?NVhO355=sL?G@7Z476|1X;s~4=zNO)y)0>GKh@7JVeWkar!%{j=ekb!_k`oBvB#*V$)O(gb~E7|Xpna-!jAH8c5U<74xW5kkaExw4U?TiuT)?0gA$&dTV;e<v|TI{$Aong$x53WV+;!(mCM<T{*ai>7S8voOwnGwYo?jR;?BE9j=8Ua=GE;6BsDp>$#R_D&nUq2Z36Dn%v-4A%*uP2y5@d=D!Frc~3?hvItSGe1fWy3?qCso`oTn{Kk8WboCq*pKd^(Xd^?73YPEDob{nB^n}$!eMEcI(CX8&JH0VJB@*;Eiqi%W}<*THMDyq0N>a=uY9gNb?+_lsMaCO632SOHTO_I;%7S(r3}m#t^wtR#Qw4(=}_*aqPgXK<Gm9k-qfEI^BfobG}{`J)R!CyNmc^4BJ}pt%1a0^Ie1{!PR%ufsV~)S*w9<00000s-Ta4C?;uL00Ghj$OixbRUeh#vBYQl0ssI200dcD')))\\n\\nlocal_host_parity=results['dqi']==LOCAL_STOCK_DQI\\nprint('Entire local-stock/hosted DQI result equality:',local_host_parity)\\narchive=WORK/'submission.zip'\\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(archive,'w',zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED,compresslevel=6) as z:\\n    for name in sorted(EXPECTED_MEMBERS):z.write(SUB/name,name)\\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(archive) as z:\\n    assert len(z.infolist())==18 and set(z.namelist())==set(EXPECTED_MEMBERS)\\n    for name,digest in EXPECTED_MEMBERS.items():\\n        with z.open(name) as f:assert hashlib.file_digest(f,'sha256').hexdigest()==digest,name\\naudit=dict(scope='Fresh full hosted official three-task checks, fresh fixed-case diagnostics, historical local comparisons separately labelled',\\n    task_results=results,full_task_results=results,fresh_all_tasks_pass=True,all_tasks_have_full_pass_evidence=True,\\n    member_hashes=EXPECTED_MEMBERS,zip_sha256=sha256(archive),source_bundle_sha256=sha256(WORK/'source_bundle.zip'),\\n    build_times=build_times,timings=timings,local_composite_estimate=gm,observed_new_public_score=None,\\n    fixed_case_diagnostics=diagnostics,known_cases_pass=True,universal_dqi_correctness_proven=False,\\n    chemistry_manifest_sha256=sha256(SRC/'chemistry/MANIFEST.json'),dqi_manifest_sha256=sha256(SRC/'dqi/MANIFEST.json'),\\n    verifier_sha256=EXPECTED_VERIFIERS,local_stock_host_entire_dqi_result_parity=local_host_parity,\\n    common_dqi_seed=COMMON_SEED,chemistry_seed=20261029173,salt=SALT,\\n    all_three_task_generators_complete=False,competition_submission_performed=False)\\n(WORK/'reproduction_audit.json').write_text(json.dumps(audit,indent=2))\\nprint('18-member ZIP read-back PASS. Ready for independent download audit; no competition submission performed.',flush=True)\\nshutil.rmtree(SUB);shutil.rmtree(SRC)\\n\",\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"execution_count\":null}]}",
    "languageNullable": "python",
    "kernelTypeNullable": "notebook",
    "slugNullable": "qcc-888q-repair-and-native-chemistry-co-design",
    "source": "{\"metadata\":{\"kernelspec\":{\"display_name\":\"Python 3\",\"language\":\"python\",\"name\":\"python3\"},\"language_info\":{\"name\":\"python\",\"version\":\"3.13\"}},\"nbformat_minor\":4,\"nbformat\":4,\"cells\":[{\"id\":\"d578e093-e74e-444d-aaf9-8d9328fee344\",\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"# 888-qubit repair and native chemistry co-design\\n\\nThis release rebuilds **both DQI and all fifteen chemistry loaders from sources**. The inherited inverse-square-root binary is authenticated against our submitted V11 output. Our selected local hybrid estimates **22.81647**; the public Code leader observed on29October2026 was22.80621. These are different measurements: a local estimate is not a new competition score.\\n\\nOur contribution combines compiler-constrained training of46angle words, physical/LP coefficient optimization, independent native plan emission, controlled component selection, and transfer of our node-policy repair to a new decoder architecture. The **three ANDs saved per traversal are credited to Heliosli(two) and Dmitrii Gluzdov(one)**. The new889Q architecture comes from SomeJoint and its credited contributors; our policy yields888Q and passes the two previously recorded regressions.\\n\\nThe following cells run fresh full official checks for all three tasks. No cached task result replaces a check. The notebook does not submit to the competition automatically.\\n\",\"metadata\":{}},{\"id\":\"244c1eb1-31e8-4fef-a186-5655ae259dd9\",\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"source\":\"import base64,gc,hashlib,importlib.util,io,json,lzma,math,os,pathlib,shutil,subprocess,sys,tempfile,time,zipfile\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport pandas as pd\\nfrom IPython.display import display\\nINPUT=pathlib.Path('/kaggle/input'); WORK=pathlib.Path('/kaggle/working')\\nCOMP=next(p.parents[2] for p in INPUT.rglob('verify_submission_invsqrt.py') if p.parents[2].name=='google-verifiable-quantum-circuit-compilation')\\nsys.path[:0]=[str(COMP/'kickmix'),str(COMP/'verifiers')]\\nimport kickmix as km\\ndef sha256(path):\\n    with open(path,'rb') as f:return hashlib.file_digest(f,'sha256').hexdigest()\\nSUB=pathlib.Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='qcc-888-submission-'))\\nSRC=pathlib.Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='qcc-888-source-'))\\nEXPECTED_MEMBERS={'dfthcsos/angle_k_0.kmb': '18d80b348ab203c243109522a3ad5eeedb1f122614ba3b0d102c3caad0f2f778', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_1.kmb': 'fa450fe53be790e293b90529403de88b6e34eb936eff212a842322869459f67d', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_10.kmb': 'e75f6b0685d754bf76f3f4d62589bf1d07b118faeeb0ab8745833733286db2fc', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_11.kmb': '773e54f6f0d7c3f769db433f263d541cdcff1076fb75109740907e3249996141', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_12.kmb': 'd86ca7ddd984059ded765b953cc936388517a7ca5789676ae90910a2be89769d', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_13.kmb': '50d82cf65116f06c0fe469ebba312f72675b277263461ab88b4d15eca947c050', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_14.kmb': 'bc42c7ffe6b2949f2b298545aacf0d9e8484f67368c6b39b2634bc60310ea236', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_2.kmb': 'c5caa2d96c44631df73d64c47e89e69114bdaf11ee2cab214a4268ea2a04d023', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_3.kmb': 'd3f67a523bfbb6e0a1bbba60768195d14e71bbc4a1fad02146960568766e279d', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_4.kmb': '27b87f755b0c4bf1fbce22316d31adaa4c5e01afd0f8cb373c978eea28143864', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_5.kmb': 'a1e3d8ef5d9188823a080d96245485725f1a4f90a3de459ee38edeea51cf8d76', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_6.kmb': '7fd7bd333b1427ecf546b0c27717ed9428e255e5165c4db14e5f95f8af45c838', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_7.kmb': '809a775b98836ee00e8783d3f616bb8517bb3a3621978bc704d20b543a8df4ec', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_8.kmb': '1cf9f7aa70e087d4402293ad95507c6fa638879eccfb757ba9f3798e24e1c27a', 'dfthcsos/angle_k_9.kmb': 'f1c49e7cf8e4f3a9adaffe167d2bbe21497a52eca2c7d09f765fc5a125e304c3', 'dfthcsos/submission.npz': 'fa84c57c00f137eb0633d07a487e154d234d2c1e92a44dc42f849b04ef60ab37', 'dqi.kmb': '736f3055850794c6beaedf8de5f7dafa1c270e2b57edd403ffa96abf6d207741', 'invsqrt.kmb': '9a8627c812833a6feca6eb82239f38d1a9a5e1eee299a9a7af9abd85e36339be'}\\nSOURCE_MANIFEST_SHA='981d6dced2adf54b0d669a2743e57f08189cdfe098a58b85dffa5bc76a9c9c5b'\\n\\nsource_manifests=[p for p in INPUT.rglob('qcc888_source_manifest.json') if sha256(p)==SOURCE_MANIFEST_SHA]\\nassert len(source_manifests)==1,'Attach QCC Native Chemistry and 888Q Source Bank; exact source manifest required'\\nsource_manifest_path=source_manifests[0]\\nBUNDLE_HASHES=json.loads(source_manifest_path.read_text())['files']\\nfor name,digest in BUNDLE_HASHES.items():\\n    q=pathlib.PurePosixPath(name)\\n    assert not q.is_absolute() and '..' not in q.parts and not name.endswith('.kmb')\\n    source=source_manifest_path.parent/name\\n    assert sha256(source)==digest,name\\n    dest=SRC/name;dest.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);shutil.copyfile(source,dest)\\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(WORK/'source_bundle.zip','w',zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED) as z:\\n    for name in sorted(BUNDLE_HASHES):z.write(SRC/name,name)\\n    z.write(source_manifest_path,'qcc888_source_manifest.json')\\nPARENT_ZIP_SHA='8095aa9c05efc789fa538af385829f9af6f699580aa832f5332f0214d1960396'\\nparents=[p for p in INPUT.rglob('submission.zip') if sha256(p)==PARENT_ZIP_SHA]\\nassert len(parents)==1,'Attach our V11/run363403318 output: exact parent ZIP required'\\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(parents[0]) as z:\\n    inv=z.read('invsqrt.kmb')\\n    assert hashlib.sha256(inv).hexdigest()==EXPECTED_MEMBERS['invsqrt.kmb']\\n    (SUB/'invsqrt.kmb').write_bytes(inv)\\nMANIFEST={'files':[{'file':n,'sha256':h} for n,h in EXPECTED_MEMBERS.items()]}\\nprint('Authenticated',len(BUNDLE_HASHES),'source/evidence files; no compiled teachers in the source payload. Inverse inherited by exact hash.',flush=True)\\n\",\"metadata\":{\"_kg_hide-input\":true},\"outputs\":[],\"execution_count\":null},{\"id\":\"1163d62c-a7b8-4b18-bc96-1dbce6c74718\",\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"## Rebuild the selected circuits\\n\\nThe chemistry bank contains the learned factor, fifteen coefficient plans, our native emitter, attribution notices and the factor-bound phase-proof evidence. It is a derived compiler research bank, not independent molecular measurements. The selected factor has \u03bb_eff48.5596378465, and the inherited product reductions lower4173\u21924170ANDs per traversal,16276\u219216270totalToffolis at430qubits.\\n\\nFor DQI, the source packet is unchanged. Our wrapper sets homogeneous groups `{7,10..16}` **before** upstream functions clone their namespaces; groups8/9 use the ordinary path. The upstream public control rebuild was byte-exact locally. The repair was independently rebuilt with stock Kickmix without a KMB input. Each hosted build below must match its precommitted circuit hash.\\n\",\"metadata\":{}},{\"id\":\"febe5aed-83a6-4264-807b-23c93f8c819f\",\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"source\":\"env={**os.environ,'PYTHONPATH':os.pathsep.join([str(COMP/'kickmix'),str(COMP/'verifiers')]),'PYTHONNOUSERSITE':'1','PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE':'1'}\\nbuild_times={}\\nfor label,command in [\\n    ('chemistry',[sys.executable,str(SRC/'chemistry/rebuild_native.py'),'--out',str(SRC/'chemistry-build')]),\\n    ('dqi',[sys.executable,str(SRC/'dqi/rebuild_dqi.py'),'--policy','repair','--runtime','stock','--out',str(SRC/'dqi-build')])]:\\n    start=time.monotonic();print('Building',label,'from authenticated source',flush=True)\\n    subprocess.run(command,check=True,env=env)\\n    build_times[label]=time.monotonic()-start\\nshutil.copytree(SRC/'chemistry-build/dfthcsos',SUB/'dfthcsos')\\nshutil.copyfile(SRC/'dqi-build/dqi.kmb',SUB/'dqi.kmb')\\nassert {p.relative_to(SUB).as_posix() for p in SUB.rglob('*') if p.is_file()}==set(EXPECTED_MEMBERS)\\nfor name,digest in EXPECTED_MEMBERS.items():assert sha256(SUB/name)==digest,name\\nprint('All18 selected member hashes match the independently verified local candidate',flush=True)\\n\",\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"execution_count\":null},{\"id\":\"9da9fea9-fb2e-4c01-99c5-bc92277f4880\",\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"source\":\"# Unchanged public Google Quantum AI metric source (Apache-2.0).\\n# https://www.kaggle.com/code/metric/google-quantum-ai-metric\\nMETRIC_SOURCE = '\\\"\\\"\\\"Kaggle metric for 161954: verifiable quantum circuit compilation benchmarks.\\\\n\\\\nA submission is an archive holding one entry per benchmark, with every circuit in either the text\\\\n(.kmx) or the binary (.kmb) kickmix format:\\\\n\\\\n    invsqrt.kmx or invsqrt.kmb   Benchmark I: phasing by beta / sqrt(x), at n_p = 10.\\\\n    dqi.kmx or dqi.kmb           Benchmark II: the DQI Reed-Solomon decoder, RS(4095, 4025) over GF(2^12).\\\\n    dfthcsos/                    Benchmark III: the DFTHC-SOS block encoding of FeMoCo76o113e, as the\\\\n                                 ANGLE_k circuits angle_k_0 ... angle_k_<n-1>, each .kmx or .kmb,\\\\n                                 and submission.npz, holding the factorization and the Givens tree.\\\\n\\\\nEach benchmark is checked by its verifier, from the competition data, which simulates the circuits on many test inputs,\\\\nrejects the submission if any test fails, and otherwise returns its cost (lower is better). Each\\\\nleaderboard split seeds the simulations with its own secret salt, so every benchmark is verified once\\\\nper split. A split\\\\'s score is the geometric mean over the benchmarks of `baseline_cost / cost`: the\\\\nhosts\\\\' reference submissions score 1.0, and halving every benchmark\\\\'s cost scores 2.0.\\\\n\\\\nThe verifiers and kickmix come from the competition data itself, attached to the metric, so it scores\\\\nwith exactly the files participants download: verifiers/ and kickmix/, built by the 161954 prep\\\\npipeline from pinned commits of the hosts\\\\' code and Qualtran. kickmix.so is compiled for that\\\\nbuild\\\\'s Kaggle image, so the metric must run in that same image. To run the metric locally instead,\\\\ninstall kickmix and the verifiers; local installs take precedence over the competition data.\\\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\\\n\\\\nimport json\\\\nimport math\\\\nimport pathlib\\\\nimport random\\\\nimport stat\\\\nimport sys\\\\nimport time\\\\nimport tokenize\\\\nimport zipfile\\\\nimport zlib\\\\nfrom collections.abc import Callable, Mapping\\\\nfrom typing import Any\\\\n\\\\nimport numpy as np\\\\nimport pandas as pd\\\\n\\\\n# kickmix/ and verifiers/ in the competition data, at the 161954 prep pipeline\\\\'s COMPETITION_DATA_MOUNT.\\\\nKICKMIX_DIR = \\\\'/kaggle/input/competitions/google-verifiable-quantum-circuit-compilation/kickmix\\\\'\\\\nVERIFIERS_DIR = \\\\'/kaggle/input/competitions/google-verifiable-quantum-circuit-compilation/verifiers\\\\'\\\\n# Where the orchestrator, and run_metric_locally, put the solution and metadata files.\\\\nEVAL_INPUTS_DIR = pathlib.Path(\\\\'/kaggle/input/competition_evaluation\\\\')\\\\n\\\\n# Every kickmix instruction, as named by Circuit.operation_statistics. Listing them rejects any\\\\n# instruction a future Qualtran adds until it is reviewed. INFO_TAG is a no-op in simulation;\\\\n# kickmix\\\\'s CircuitBuilder emits it around every iadd and isub. DEBUG_PRINT is a no-op too, as every\\\\n# verifier\\\\'s simulator ignores it, but its qubit and bit ids still count toward the circuit\\\\'s.\\\\nALLOWED_INSTRUCTIONS = {\\\\n    \\\\'X\\\\', \\\\'CX\\\\', \\\\'CCX\\\\', \\\\'Z\\\\', \\\\'CZ\\\\', \\\\'CCZ\\\\', \\\\'Z_POW\\\\', \\\\'NEG\\\\', \\\\'SWAP\\\\', \\\\'CSWAP\\\\', \\\\'R\\\\', \\\\'HMR\\\\', \\\\'BIT_INVERT\\\\', \\\\'BIT_STORE0\\\\', \\\\'BIT_STORE1\\\\',\\\\n    \\\\'PUSH_CONDITION\\\\', \\\\'POP_CONDITION\\\\', \\\\'INFO_TAG\\\\', \\\\'DEBUG_PRINT\\\\',\\\\n}  # fmt: skip\\\\n# Qubit and bit ids must be below this. Verifier memory grew by ~1.5 KB per bit (dqi) and ~1.1 KB\\\\n# per qubit (invsqrt) with the verifiers at c636a96, so this capped the growth at ~1 GB; at 03027f8,\\\\n# dqi\\\\'s grows by only ~0.2 KB per qubit or bit, linearly rather than with their product. The\\\\n# baselines use ids below 50,000. Raise it if a harder benchmark needs more.\\\\nMAX_QUBIT_OR_BIT_ID = 2**30 // 1536\\\\n# The arrays read from a dfthcsos submission.npz may total at most this many bytes, ~30 times the\\\\n# ~2 MB the reference factorization and tree take.\\\\nMAX_NPZ_BYTES = 2**26\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nclass ParticipantVisibleError(Exception):\\\\n    pass\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef read_circuit(path: pathlib.Path, max_registers: int) -> Any:\\\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return a submitted .kmx or .kmb circuit as a kickmix.Circuit; raise ValueError unless it is fit to verify.\\\\n\\\\n    kickmix validates a file as it parses it, within limits that keep parsing cheap, but simulating\\\\n    takes memory that grows with the largest qubit and bit ids, which kickmix allows up to ~5e8,\\\\n    so those are capped at MAX_QUBIT_OR_BIT_ID. kickmix also allows a million registers, at\\\\n    ~110 bytes each even if empty, so a circuit may have at most `max_registers`, the most its\\\\n    benchmark needs. Every register must be named: the dfthcsos verifier crashes on an unnamed one.\\\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\\\n    import kickmix  # ty: ignore[unresolved-import]  # In kickmix/, which generate_standard_submission put on sys.path.\\\\n\\\\n    circuit = kickmix.Circuit.from_file(path, format=path.suffix.removeprefix(\\\\'.\\\\'))\\\\n    unsupported = set(circuit.operation_statistics()) - ALLOWED_INSTRUCTIONS\\\\n    if unsupported:\\\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\\'unsupported instructions {sorted(unsupported)}\\\\')\\\\n    largest_id = max(circuit.num_qubits, circuit.num_bits) - 1\\\\n    if largest_id >= MAX_QUBIT_OR_BIT_ID:\\\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\\'qubit or bit id {largest_id} is above the limit of {MAX_QUBIT_OR_BIT_ID - 1}\\\\')\\\\n    if circuit.num_registers > max_registers:\\\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\\'{circuit.num_registers} registers, above the limit of {max_registers} for this benchmark\\\\')\\\\n    if not all(isinstance(name, str) for name in circuit.register_data):\\\\n        raise ValueError(\\\\'every register needs a name, given by its REGISTER line\\\\')\\\\n    return circuit\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef read_npz(path: pathlib.Path, spec: Mapping[str, tuple[str, tuple[int | str, ...]]]) -> dict[str, np.ndarray]:\\\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return the arrays `spec` names from an .npz; raise ValueError unless each is a plain number array as specified.\\\\n\\\\n    `spec` maps each key to the numpy dtype kinds it may have, such as \\\\'f\\\\' for floats, and its shape,\\\\n    in which a string names a dimension of any positive size that must agree wherever it recurs.\\\\n\\\\n    Each array\\\\'s header is a Python literal of its dtype and shape, which np.load trusts: a few KB\\\\n    of deflated zeros can claim a terabyte-sized array, and the dtype can be anything numpy can\\\\n    describe, from structured and nested types to Python objects that need unpickling. So the\\\\n    headers are read first, and the arrays loaded only if each is a plain number type of its kind,\\\\n    not big-endian, with its shape, and they total at most MAX_NPZ_BYTES. Only format 1.0 headers,\\\\n    which numpy.savez writes, are accepted, and numpy refuses any over 10 KB before parsing it.\\\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\\\n    dimensions: dict[str, int] = {}\\\\n    total = 0\\\\n    with zipfile.ZipFile(path) as archive:\\\\n        members = {name.removesuffix(\\\\'.npy\\\\'): name for name in archive.namelist()}\\\\n        missing = [key for key in spec if key not in members]\\\\n        if missing:\\\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\\'{path.name} has no {missing}\\\\')\\\\n        for key, (kinds, expected_shape) in spec.items():\\\\n            with archive.open(members[key]) as member:\\\\n                if np.lib.format.read_magic(member) != (1, 0):\\\\n                    raise ValueError(f\\\\'{key} in {path.name} is not in .npy format 1.0, which numpy.savez writes\\\\')\\\\n                shape, _, dtype = np.lib.format.read_array_header_1_0(member)\\\\n            if dtype.kind not in kinds or dtype.names is not None or dtype.subdtype is not None or dtype.byteorder == \\\\'>\\\\':\\\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\\'{key} in {path.name} has dtype {dtype}, not a plain number type of numpy kind {kinds!r}\\\\')\\\\n            matches = len(shape) == len(expected_shape) and all(\\\\n                size > 0 and size == (dimensions.setdefault(expected, size) if isinstance(expected, str) else expected)\\\\n                for size, expected in zip(shape, expected_shape, strict=True)\\\\n            )\\\\n            if not matches:\\\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\\'{key} in {path.name} has shape {shape}, not {expected_shape} with its named dimensions as in {dimensions}\\\\')\\\\n            total += math.prod(shape) * dtype.itemsize\\\\n    if total > MAX_NPZ_BYTES:\\\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\\'the arrays in {path.name} take {total:,} bytes, above the limit of {MAX_NPZ_BYTES:,}\\\\')\\\\n    with np.load(path, allow_pickle=False) as npz:\\\\n        return {key: np.array(npz[key]) for key in spec}\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef find_one(root: pathlib.Path, name: str, description: str, is_dir: bool = False) -> pathlib.Path:\\\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The one path called `name` (a glob) under `root`, where the submission unpacked; raise ParticipantVisibleError otherwise.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\\\n    # macOS Finder\\\\'s Compress adds __MACOSX/, which mirrors every directory, with an AppleDouble ._ file per file.\\\\n    paths = [path for path in root.rglob(name) if path.is_dir() == is_dir and \\\\'__MACOSX\\\\' not in path.relative_to(root).parts]\\\\n    if len(paths) != 1:\\\\n        raise ParticipantVisibleError(f\\\\'The submission must contain exactly one {description}, found {len(paths)}.\\\\')\\\\n    return paths[0]\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef generate_standard_submission(submission_dir: str) -> None:\\\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Verify the submission under every split\\\\'s salt, and write each verification\\\\'s cost as submission.csv.\\\\n\\\\n    `submission_dir` is where the orchestrator unpacked the submission archive. Every split\\\\'s verifications run here, in random order, before the orchestrator calls score() for\\\\n    either split, so neither a failure\\\\'s timing nor its message shows which split it failed on.\\\\n    Every file is read and checked before any verifier runs, so a malformed file fails in seconds\\\\n    rather than after another benchmark\\\\'s verification. The verifiers run one at a time, as the\\\\n    invsqrt and dqi verifiers spread their own simulation across processes.\\\\n\\\\n    The orchestrator passes neither the solution nor the metadata in, so the solution is read from\\\\n    where it puts it; this metric\\\\'s own solution names its row id column `row_id`. Each row\\\\'s\\\\n    `seed_salt` is merged by its verifier with the submission\\\\'s hash to seed the simulation, so a\\\\n    submission always faces the same tests, but participants can\\\\'t compute them. Unsalted, the seed\\\\n    would let a team whose circuit fails on a few inputs re-roll its tests offline with cost-free\\\\n    edits until they miss those inputs; with the salt, each re-roll costs a submission. A salt that\\\\n    is missing or short is refused, as it would leave the seed unsalted or guessable.\\\\n\\\\n    kickmix and the verifiers are imported here rather than at the top because the orchestrator imports\\\\n    this module during validation, when the competition data isn\\\\'t mounted.\\\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\\\n    solution_paths = list(EVAL_INPUTS_DIR.glob(\\\\'solution.*\\\\'))\\\\n    if len(solution_paths) != 1:\\\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\\'Expected one solution.csv or solution.parquet in {EVAL_INPUTS_DIR}, found {[path.name for path in solution_paths]}\\\\')\\\\n    [solution_path] = solution_paths\\\\n    solution = pd.read_csv(solution_path) if solution_path.suffix == \\\\'.csv\\\\' else pd.read_parquet(solution_path)\\\\n    scored = solution[solution[\\\\'Usage\\\\'] != \\\\'Ignored\\\\']\\\\n    # score()\\\\'s hyperparameters, which the orchestrator passes only to score().\\\\n    hyperparameters = json.loads((EVAL_INPUTS_DIR / \\\\'metadata.json\\\\').read_text()).get(\\\\'Hyperparameters\\\\') or {}\\\\n    shot_divisor = int(hyperparameters.get(\\\\'verification_shot_divisor\\\\', 1))\\\\n    for salt in scored[\\\\'seed_salt\\\\']:\\\\n        if not isinstance(salt, str) or len(salt) < 32:\\\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\\'Every scored solution row needs a seed_salt of at least 32 characters, got {salt!r}\\\\')\\\\n\\\\n    # Appended, not prepended, so local installs of kickmix and the verifiers win when running locally.\\\\n    sys.path += [KICKMIX_DIR, VERIFIERS_DIR]\\\\n    from dfthcsos import verify as dfthcsos_verify  # ty: ignore[unresolved-import]  # These live in verifiers/.\\\\n    from dfthcsos.scoreinfra.reference import FACTORIZATION_KEYS, ORBITALS  # ty: ignore[unresolved-import]\\\\n    from dqi import verify_submission_dqi  # ty: ignore[unresolved-import]\\\\n    from invsqrt import verify_submission_invsqrt  # ty: ignore[unresolved-import]\\\\n\\\\n    root = pathlib.Path(submission_dir)\\\\n\\\\n    def read(path: pathlib.Path, reader: Callable[[pathlib.Path, Any], Any], spec: Any) -> Any:\\\\n        # tar and 7z submissions can unpack links, which would have this read the host\\\\'s files, and\\\\n        # FIFOs and devices, which would block or never end.\\\\n        status = path.lstat()\\\\n        if not stat.S_ISREG(status.st_mode) or status.st_nlink > 1 or not path.resolve().is_relative_to(root.resolve()):\\\\n            raise ParticipantVisibleError(f\\\\'{path.relative_to(root)} must be a regular file, not a link or a special file.\\\\')\\\\n        try:\\\\n            return reader(path, spec)\\\\n        # What kickmix, zipfile, zlib and numpy raise on malformed files, found by fuzzing an .npz.\\\\n        except (ValueError, RuntimeError, OSError, EOFError, zipfile.BadZipFile, zlib.error, tokenize.TokenError) as err:\\\\n            raise ParticipantVisibleError(f\\\\'{path.relative_to(root)} is invalid: {err}\\\\') from err\\\\n\\\\n    batches = max(1, verify_submission_dqi.DEFAULT_NUM_SHOTS // verify_submission_dqi.DEFAULT_BATCH_SIZE // shot_divisor)\\\\n    dqi_spec = verify_submission_dqi.ProblemSpecDQI.benchmark_instance(num_shots=batches * verify_submission_dqi.DEFAULT_BATCH_SIZE)\\\\n    # Each circuit\\\\'s most registers: invsqrt\\\\'s x, and dqi\\\\'s S_i and E_j.\\\\n    invsqrt = read(find_one(root, \\\\'invsqrt.km[xb]\\\\', \\\\'invsqrt.kmx or invsqrt.kmb\\\\'), read_circuit, 1)\\\\n    dqi = read(find_one(root, \\\\'dqi.km[xb]\\\\', \\\\'dqi.kmx or dqi.kmb\\\\'), read_circuit, dqi_spec.n + dqi_spec.m)\\\\n    dfthcsos_dir = find_one(root, \\\\'dfthcsos\\\\', \\\\'dfthcsos directory\\\\', is_dir=True)\\\\n    angle_files = list(dfthcsos_dir.glob(\\\\'angle_k_*.km[xb]\\\\'))\\\\n    angle_paths = {path.stem: path for path in angle_files}\\\\n    # A circuit given in both formats leaves fewer stems than files, so the two can\\\\'t match.\\\\n    stems = [f\\\\'angle_k_{k}\\\\' for k in range(len(angle_files))]\\\\n    if not stems or sorted(angle_paths) != sorted(stems):\\\\n        raise ParticipantVisibleError(\\\\'dfthcsos/ must hold the circuits angle_k_0 ... angle_k_<n-1>, each once, as .kmx or .kmb.\\\\')\\\\n    # An ANGLE_k circuit\\\\'s `selection` and `word_j` registers each hold a qubit, of at most QUBIT_CAP.\\\\n    # The verifier allows other registers too, but none are needed.\\\\n    angle_circuits = [read(angle_paths[stem], read_circuit, dfthcsos_verify.QUBIT_CAP) for stem in stems]\\\\n    # The factorization (see dfthcsos.scoreinfra.reference), with R factors of B vectors over the N\\\\n    # orbitals and C copies, and the Givens tree\\\\'s N - 1 edges.\\\\n    npz_spec = {\\\\n        \\\\'U\\\\': (\\\\'f\\\\', (\\\\'R\\\\', \\\\'B\\\\', ORBITALS)),\\\\n        \\\\'W\\\\': (\\\\'f\\\\', (\\\\'R\\\\', \\\\'B\\\\', \\\\'C\\\\')),\\\\n        \\\\'H2_I\\\\': (\\\\'f\\\\', (\\\\'R\\\\', \\\\'C\\\\')),\\\\n        \\\\'H1_I\\\\': (\\\\'f\\\\', ()),\\\\n        \\\\'Hsym_lower\\\\': (\\\\'f\\\\', (ORBITALS * (ORBITALS + 1) // 2,)),\\\\n        \\\\'tree_edges\\\\': (\\\\'iu\\\\', (ORBITALS - 1, 2)),\\\\n    }\\\\n    if set(npz_spec) != {*FACTORIZATION_KEYS, \\\\'tree_edges\\\\'}:\\\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\\'The dfthcsos verifier reads the factorization arrays {FACTORIZATION_KEYS}, which npz_spec must cover exactly\\\\')\\\\n    npz = read(find_one(dfthcsos_dir, \\\\'submission.npz\\\\', \\\\'dfthcsos/submission.npz\\\\'), read_npz, npz_spec)\\\\n    tree_edges = npz.pop(\\\\'tree_edges\\\\')\\\\n\\\\n    # Benchmark -> its verifier run, given the salt.\\\\n    verifications: dict[str, Callable[[str], dict[str, Any]]] = {\\\\n        \\\\'invsqrt\\\\': lambda salt: verify_submission_invsqrt.verify(invsqrt, verify_submission_invsqrt.ProblemSpecInvSqrt.for_n_p(10), salt=salt),\\\\n        \\\\'dqi\\\\': lambda salt: verify_submission_dqi.verify(dqi, dqi_spec, salt=salt),\\\\n        \\\\'dfthcsos\\\\': lambda salt: dfthcsos_verify.verify(\\\\n            angle_circuits, npz, tree_edges, salt=salt, shots_per_address=max(1, dfthcsos_verify.SHOTS_PER_ADDRESS // shot_divisor)\\\\n        ),\\\\n    }\\\\n    runs = list(zip(scored[\\\\'row_id\\\\'], scored[\\\\'benchmark\\\\'], scored[\\\\'seed_salt\\\\'], strict=True))\\\\n    random.shuffle(runs)\\\\n    # Ignored rows aren\\\\'t scored, but the orchestrator still expects a submission row for each.\\\\n    costs, seconds = dict.fromkeys(solution[\\\\'row_id\\\\'], 0.0), dict.fromkeys(solution[\\\\'row_id\\\\'], 0.0)\\\\n    for row_id, benchmark, salt in runs:\\\\n        start = time.monotonic()\\\\n        try:\\\\n            costs[row_id] = float(verifications[benchmark](salt)[\\\\'score\\\\'])\\\\n        # The exceptions the verifiers\\\\' command lines report as a failed submission; dfthcsos\\\\'s\\\\n        # InvalidCircuits is a ValueError.\\\\n        except (AssertionError, ValueError, RuntimeError, KeyError) as err:\\\\n            raise ParticipantVisibleError(f\\\\'The {benchmark} submission failed verification: {err}\\\\') from err\\\\n        if not costs[row_id] > 0:\\\\n            raise ParticipantVisibleError(f\\\\'The {benchmark} submission has non-positive cost {costs[row_id]}.\\\\')\\\\n        seconds[row_id] = time.monotonic() - start\\\\n    pd.DataFrame({\\\\'row_id\\\\': list(costs), \\\\'cost\\\\': list(costs.values()), \\\\'seconds\\\\': list(seconds.values())}).to_csv(\\\\'submission.csv\\\\', index=False)\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef score(\\\\n    solution: pd.DataFrame, submission: pd.DataFrame, row_id_column_name: str, verification_shot_divisor: int = 1\\\\n) -> tuple[float, dict[str, Any]]:\\\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return the geometric mean over the benchmarks of `baseline_cost / cost`, where higher is better.\\\\n\\\\n    `verification_shot_divisor` is for testing only, and must stay 1 on Kaggle. generate_standard_submission\\\\n    reads it, and divides the dqi and dfthcsos verifiers\\\\' default numbers of shots by it, which makes\\\\n    their verification that much faster and weaker, and changes their costs, so that the reference\\\\n    submissions no longer score 1.0. invsqrt\\\\'s verifier is the fastest, and needs a multiple of 64\\\\n    shots per input to fill its batches, its default, so it keeps every shot.\\\\n\\\\n    The solution has a row per benchmark and leaderboard split, holding the split\\\\'s secret\\\\n    `seed_salt` and the `baseline_cost` its benchmark\\\\'s reference submission scored under that salt.\\\\n    `submission` is generate_standard_submission\\\\'s output, which holds each row\\\\'s `cost`, as the\\\\n    verification runs there. Returns each benchmark\\\\'s cost, improvement and verification time as\\\\n    details.\\\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\\\n    merged = solution.merge(submission, on=row_id_column_name, validate=\\\\'one_to_one\\\\')\\\\n    details = {\\\\n        benchmark: {\\\\'cost\\\\': cost, \\\\'improvement_over_baseline\\\\': baseline_cost / cost, \\\\'seconds\\\\': run_seconds}\\\\n        for benchmark, cost, baseline_cost, run_seconds in zip(\\\\n            merged[\\\\'benchmark\\\\'], merged[\\\\'cost\\\\'], merged[\\\\'baseline_cost\\\\'], merged[\\\\'seconds\\\\'], strict=True\\\\n        )\\\\n    }\\\\n    ratios = [benchmark_details[\\\\'improvement_over_baseline\\\\'] for benchmark_details in details.values()]\\\\n    return math.prod(ratios) ** (1 / len(ratios)), details\\\\n'\\n\\nimport importlib.util, gc\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport pandas as pd\\nfrom IPython.display import display\\nmetric_path = WORK / 'official_metric_readers.py'\\nmetric_path.write_text(METRIC_SOURCE, encoding='utf-8')\\nspec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('official_metric', metric_path)\\nmetric = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\\nspec.loader.exec_module(metric)\\nnpz_spec = {'U': ('f', ('R', 'B', 76)), 'W': ('f', ('R', 'B', 'C')),\\n            'H2_I': ('f', ('R', 'C')), 'H1_I': ('f', ()),\\n            'Hsym_lower': ('f', (2926,)), 'tree_edges': ('iu', (75, 2))}\\nparams = metric.read_npz(SUB / 'dfthcsos/submission.npz', npz_spec)\\nreader_rows = []\\nfor item in MANIFEST['files']:\\n    name = item['file']\\n    if not name.endswith('.kmb'):\\n        continue\\n    cap = 1 if name == 'invsqrt.kmb' else 4165 if name == 'dqi.kmb' else 128\\n    circ = metric.read_circuit(SUB / name, cap)\\n    reader_rows.append({'file': name, 'qubits': int(circ.num_qubits),\\n                        'static_Toffoli': int(circ.operation_statistics().num_toffoli_like),\\n                        'sha256': item['sha256']})\\n    del circ\\n    gc.collect()\\nassert len(reader_rows) == 17 and len(MANIFEST['files']) == 18\\nassert {r['file'] for r in reader_rows if r['file'].startswith('dfthcsos/')} == {\\n    f'dfthcsos/angle_k_{i}.kmb' for i in range(15)}\\nprint('Official input readers: PASS; factor shapes', {k: list(v.shape) for k,v in params.items()})\\npd.DataFrame(reader_rows).to_csv(WORK / 'member_hashes.csv', index=False)\\n\",\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"execution_count\":null},{\"id\":\"699d0014-6a44-475a-adc5-1deb5b3aaf65\",\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"## Fresh complete official verification\\n\\nThe official verifier sources and default shot counts stay unchanged. Chemistry checks78080shots, DQI102400shots, and inverse-square-root every3133452legal input64times (200540928shots). DQI uses the precommitted common seed2026102801; chemistry uses20261029173. These explicit seeds support controlled reproduction and are not the hidden competition salts. No seed search, shot reduction or failure-rate substitution is used.\\n\\nLocal stock/fork results already agreed in every result field at the common seed. A second independent full DQI seed, both recorded regressions and a36-weight stress grid also passed locally. Those are historical evidence; the following full checks and later fixed-case rows are fresh on this Kaggle host.\\n\",\"metadata\":{}},{\"id\":\"bbc2b4bd-cbf4-4446-8cbc-d0ef814f859f\",\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"source\":\"EXPECTED_VERIFIERS={'dqi': 'f14274bc0943fb9769ddb01131be6063191a15009fe1caf1d4bdd9fd25194e65', 'invsqrt': 'ddef520dec6b68d1cf0a6f328ddd36d79eb84570b9192cf3f7acaf073f06733a', 'dfthcsos': '0775be7a528922367caebe9e4d051d6199811f1aefeaa4b793eaaa4621b8ec9d'}\\n\\nfor task,filename in [('dqi','dqi/verify_submission_dqi.py'),('invsqrt','invsqrt/verify_submission_invsqrt.py'),('dfthcsos','dfthcsos/verify.py')]:\\n    assert sha256(COMP/'verifiers'/filename)==EXPECTED_VERIFIERS[task],('Verifier changed',task)\\nfrom dfthcsos import verify as vdft\\nfrom dqi import verify_submission_dqi as DQI\\nfrom invsqrt.verify_submission_invsqrt import verify as verify_inv,ProblemSpecInvSqrt,N_P\\nSALT='notebook-verification'; COMMON_SEED=2026102801\\nresults={};timings={}\\nfor task in ['dfthcsos','dqi','invsqrt']:\\n    start=time.monotonic();print('Starting FULL',task,flush=True)\\n    if task=='dfthcsos':result=vdft.verify(str(SUB/'dfthcsos'),salt=SALT,seed=20261029173)\\n    else:\\n        c=km.Circuit.from_file(SUB/(task+'.kmb'),format='kmb')\\n        result=(DQI.verify(c,DQI.ProblemSpecDQI.benchmark_instance(),salt=SALT,seed=COMMON_SEED) if task=='dqi'\\n                else verify_inv(c,ProblemSpecInvSqrt.for_n_p(N_P),salt=SALT))\\n        del c;gc.collect()\\n    assert result['status']=='PASS',(task,result)\\n    assert result['verified_shots']=={'dfthcsos':78080,'dqi':102400,'invsqrt':200540928}[task]\\n    results[task]=result;timings[task]=time.monotonic()-start\\n    (WORK/(task+'_full_result.json')).write_text(json.dumps(result,indent=2))\\n    print(task,'FULL PASS cost',result['score'],'seconds',round(timings[task],2),flush=True)\\nassert results['dqi']['value_errors']==results['dqi']['phase_errors']==0 and results['dqi']['num_qubits']==888\\nassert results['dqi']['circuit_sha256']==EXPECTED_MEMBERS['dqi.kmb']\\nassert results['invsqrt']['circuit_sha256']==EXPECTED_MEMBERS['invsqrt.kmb']\\nassert results['dfthcsos']['toffoli_count']==16270 and results['dfthcsos']['num_qubits']==430\\nassert math.isclose(results['dfthcsos']['score'],339728082.3378603,rel_tol=2e-12)\\nREF={'invsqrt':2076774.233715282,'dqi':24439463583672.93,'dfthcsos':3355599588.3155375}\\ngm=math.prod(REF[t]/results[t]['score'] for t in REF)**(1/3)\\nprint('Fresh full three-task local GM',gm,'; not an observed competition public score',flush=True)\\ndisplay(pd.DataFrame([dict(task=t,cost=r['score'],Q=r['num_qubits'],T=r.get('toffoli_count'),shots=r['verified_shots'],seconds=timings[t]) for t,r in results.items()]))\\n\",\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"execution_count\":null},{\"id\":\"afb159a2-840c-46f4-b9dc-8f610a72aaac\",\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"## Fixed-input regression tests\\n\\nRepeat two synthetic logical inputs256times under each of two simulator seeds. Changed syndromes or dirty ancilla count as value errors; a wrong phase with correct values counts separately. These deliberately selected cases **cannot est