DO(30R7e0xw!OK1l)~%wU|IvN_n<p(&lNDExdKRDB312HV-i5Vcg%ldJXC^bi^#s&b_uz(l3-+Ib!Wg4@TM)zhsU(={@<akUhN-bsr1cIm$#u3jOP<)gXhe>eiVE;xMD&5JSb@AHqp#F2AWUg4I1DMDi3K)wZ)#b=3LL}>`W%26dX8bD4Z>04PJUy`5Fq#Mn!rs<`Rv#_4pI+$m+142Z#o7+SR<O2busMpyoZL0@s=ki|IJV&;-KX9&qvE_^0rfOFvS+>79!K(qn*Y9iOP-9Wx(^x{Ie3K%03LpzdTZO3$HXs565@U0imXx`;jsRiG}oCk<+A$N}5wUx-qV~Zi_AOIkP!b!9ZLLlv!cpb1gYO$0*jRF`g=a4|Yf^!dTN-+Jn^W$CUl52yLW{NEcIYlGWf@^DQKqTLWLADJ4OypM9knVl$fUxtCgiG1<bc<WB{u?;o#%PoWcV0`tIt<UCEt=h9LkQq{WBrGdYQd4eR#-fn&UZUdITo2k!d{;+s>xO%7g<%WrvnUsaX|3EwA8sKi>pPJe4s9)~}#UM6+YF!_T9yKs_GdB0A(2(W#1+~C%v~rD<lOexf8)@2>wv>`#1?$OF{g(})R5tF<7-s5_hpRibW6h(NB>3)p9|1&fgpkq&#NZt``sKXJGS<zSzr~?#`(3Wn#`;BKm(TNYRPXGDQP$cJ+)mx8jIgHjH?*b_GMzUEd+4d*nZU@>OfR=BoquyOKp->`RPd*61mC96&OPbtOgQYP8ou98j1kuWfNBaBGR;Br1?X4>yNb_Etc|Fk1h0_j1jC;G%9Z#g^53nu*(Z6RW^lX%03wiG>s-m{ez6U)*v*oMAwn`-qiOX}y`F}WPpwIUKKms=jks;m>G(-OsiY8^8`os?xO(G5)(YlUic;}6^A(v-<6hOl(UKOb^i%)<f9}6@#{!A?00FFw0nC#F`PlI~vBYQl0ssI200dcD')))\\ndef probe_case(circuit,case,seed):\\n    problem=DQI.ProblemSpecDQI.benchmark_instance()\\n    syndrome_qubits,mbuc_bits,ancilla=DQI.validate_registers(circuit,problem)\\n    syn=np.tile(np.asarray(case['syndromes'],np.int64),(256,1))\\n    mask=np.tile(np.asarray(case['mbuc_masks'],np.int64),(256,1))\\n    expected=np.full(256,case['expected_phase_flip'],bool)\\n    sim=km.Simulator(batch_size=256,debug_print=False,counting_operations=True,seed=seed)\\n    sim.use_same_registers_as(circuit)\\n    inp=DQI.to_bits(syn,problem.degree)\\n    sim.write_across_shots(km.array(syndrome_qubits),inp)\\n    sim.write_across_shots(km.array(mbuc_bits),DQI.to_bits(mask,problem.degree))\\n    sim.do(circuit)\\n    diff=sim.read_across_shots(km.array(syndrome_qubits))^inp\\n    junk=sim.read_across_shots(ancilla) if len(ancilla) else np.zeros((0,256),bool)\\n    value=diff.any(axis=0)|junk.any(axis=0)\\n    phase=(sim.read_phase_flipped_across_shots()^expected)&~value\\n    return dict(replicas=256,value_errors=int(value.sum()),phase_errors=int(phase.sum()))\\nc=km.Circuit.from_file(SUB/'dqi.kmb',format='kmb');diagnostics=[]\\nfor case in CASES:\\n    for seed in [2026102801,2026102802]:\\n        diagnostics.append(dict(case_kind=case['kind'],measurement_seed=seed,**probe_case(c,case,seed)))\\ndel c;gc.collect()\\nassert len(diagnostics)==4 and all(r['value_errors']==r['phase_errors']==0 for r in diagnostics)\\ndisplay(pd.DataFrame(diagnostics))\\npd.DataFrame(diagnostics).to_csv(WORK/'fixed_case_diagnostics.csv',index=False)\\n\",\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"execution_count\":null},{\"id\":\"9856807e-a84d-4abc-9780-908ee39f93f3\",\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"## Controlled chemistry comparison and exact proof scope\\n\\nThe following rows are **historical local full-verifier comparisons**, distinct from the fresh hosted results above. Each public/control and our candidate passed two complete checks. At the same seeds20261029173/174, Dmitrii V34 costs340123487.23, his later V35 costs339903340.03, and our selected hybrid costs339728082.34. V35 adds no new angle circuit relative to V34; its DQI is the same new public889Q file.\\n\\nThe chemistry bank also binds an exact phase/word/scratch certificate for all1220valid addresses, both reachable traversals and every2^80HMR outcome assignment per loader. Six deliberate faulty-circuit controls are rejected. The scope is the official reachable ANGLE contract; it is not an arbitrary-input circuit proof or a proof of the whole DQI decoder. Certificate sources, factor binding and historical receipts are in the source bundle.\\n\",\"metadata\":{}},{\"id\":\"de780e8d-2ef1-46f9-8c90-1c4ed25b39d6\",\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"source\":\"historical_chemistry=[{'arm': 'HeliosliV20', 'local_cost': 339980584.979305, 'seeds': '20261029171,20261029172', 'shots': 156160}, {'arm': 'OwnHeliosTwoAND', 'local_cost': 339769843.6264083, 'seeds': '20261029171,20261029172', 'shots': 156160}, {'arm': 'DmitriiV34', 'local_cost': 340123487.22578806, 'seeds': '20261029173,20261029174', 'shots': 156160}, {'arm': 'OwnThreeAND', 'local_cost': 339728082.3378603, 'seeds': '20261029173,20261029174', 'shots': 156160}, {'arm': 'DmitriiV35', 'local_cost': 339903340.0291362, 'seeds': '20261029173,20261029174', 'shots': 156160}]\\n\\ndisplay(pd.DataFrame(historical_chemistry))\\npd.DataFrame(historical_chemistry).to_csv(WORK/'historical_chemistry_comparison.csv',index=False)\\n\",\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"execution_count\":null},{\"id\":\"1e4b6030-cb1d-446b-ae58-52ec493c63c0\",\"cell_type\":\"markdown\",\"source\":\"## Artifacts and attribution\\n\\n`submission.zip` contains exactly18members. `source_bundle.zip` contains the source-only portions of the two immutable local banks, their manifests, plans, learned factor, licences and historical positive/negative evidence. It contains no KMB teacher inputs and no gated Hamiltonian target tensors. The inverse binary remains inherited; a complete inverse generator is not claimed.\\n\\n- [SomeJoint V21/run363462588](https://www.kaggle.com/code/somejoint/quantum-circuits-22-77-local-gm-889-qubit-dqi?scriptVersionId=363462588): new889Q architecture and source contributors, retained Apache-2.0 notices. Our wrapper transfers the existing node-policy repair; it does not invent the architecture.\\n- [Heliosli V20/run363468177](https://www.kaggle.com/code/heliosli/the-dataset-is-public-now-enjoy?scriptVersionId=363468177): two inherited product-plan AND reductions in angle1/8.\\n- [Dmitrii Gluzdov V34/run363471947](https://www.kaggle.com/code/dmitriigluzdov/quantum-circuit-compilation-from-source?scriptVersionId=363471947): distinct angle2 reduction and factor lineage; V35/run363498255 was also compared.\\n- [Ahmed Berat \u00d6zer](https://www.kaggle.com/code/ahmedberatozer/quantum-ai-df-thc-group-compression), mrmeows, Kirill, and other contributors named in the bundle: QR/barrier, Gram-gauge, reachable-phase auditing and earlier circuit/factor prior art. Our additional angle/factor co-design, active-L1 block LP, native emission and measured integration are recorded separately.\\n- [Busyaprime](https://www.kaggle.com/code/busyaprime/lb-22-72431-22x-cheaper-than-google-s-circuits) and the inherited mrmeows/Qualtran lineage:63Q inverse circuit authenticated through [our V11](https://www.kaggle.com/code/atakanaldemir/quantum-circuits-iso-gap-dqi-h5?scriptVersionId=363403318).\\n- [manwithacat](https://www.kaggle.com/code/manwithacat/the-real-150k-was-the-friends-we-made): failure-case and local parallel-parity tooling lineage; the hosted checks above use the official verifier directly.\\n- [Google Quantum AI metric](https://www.kaggle.com/code/metric/google-quantum-ai-metric): unchanged official readers and verifiers.\\n\\nThe local gain over public Code is small; the top10 objective still needs a larger structural improvement. Votes, medals and Code Expert are outcomes of community usefulness, not guarantees from a competition score.\\n\",\"metadata\":{}},{\"id\":\"d99e2c1e-a416-4e22-a1ff-227ec5ffcde4\",\"cell_type\":\"code\",\"source\":\"LOCAL_STOCK_DQI=json.loads(lzma.decompress(base64.b85decode('{Wp48S^xk9=GL@E0stWa761SMbT8$j-~-13HeCQch>B-}dC<MbDB9ftsJclzur<UpM_#j1yopA5*oammEl)#FXtmqsD&=T6SryGebx1tNd=3OBnMyh~wex9A60uP$vE~1I2#9uJ9Jd<*E2|W3Z!V8M*L{r3-cpiftAVByk*&jXyyiR!k%AH&QmNX?5oKdOugv+JI@VJ#R(j6eH^K(M_ixhVMGZ%jt=mUy3l3zsn*XZ73Z2cq*^0|UN_y>YKR7tS8k%QB{j<kHV&9MuptLTx)%K2YGa$?+VjlPwcq`G-r^-^ww7=ymqm_e?a0?NVhO355=sL?G@7Z476|1X;s~4=zNO)y)0>GKh@7JVeWkar!%{j=ekb!_k`oBvB#*V$)O(gb~E7|Xpna-!jAH8c5U<74xW5kkaExw4U?TiuT)?0gA$&dTV;e<v|TI{$Aong$x53WV+;!(mCM<T{*ai>7S8voOwnGwYo?jR;?BE9j=8Ua=GE;6BsDp>$#R_D&nUq2Z36Dn%v-4A%*uP2y5@d=D!Frc~3?hvItSGe1fWy3?qCso`oTn{Kk8WboCq*pKd^(Xd^?73YPEDob{nB^n}$!eMEcI(CX8&JH0VJB@*;Eiqi%W}<*THMDyq0N>a=uY9gNb?+_lsMaCO632SOHTO_I;%7S(r3}m#t^wtR#Qw4(=}_*aqPgXK<Gm9k-qfEI^BfobG}{`J)R!CyNmc^4BJ}pt%1a0^Ie1{!PR%ufsV~)S*w9<00000s-Ta4C?;uL00Ghj$OixbRUeh#vBYQl0ssI200dcD')))\\n\\nlocal_host_parity=results['dqi']==LOCAL_STOCK_DQI\\nprint('Entire local-stock/hosted DQI result equality:',local_host_parity)\\narchive=WORK/'submission.zip'\\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(archive,'w',zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED,compresslevel=6) as z:\\n    for name in sorted(EXPECTED_MEMBERS):z.write(SUB/name,name)\\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(archive) as z:\\n    assert len(z.infolist())==18 and set(z.namelist())==set(EXPECTED_MEMBERS)\\n    for name,digest in EXPECTED_MEMBERS.items():\\n        with z.open(name) as f:assert hashlib.file_digest(f,'sha256').hexdigest()==digest,name\\naudit=dict(scope='Fresh full hosted official three-task checks, fresh fixed-case diagnostics, historical local comparisons separately labelled',\\n    task_results=results,full_task_results=results,fresh_all_tasks_pass=True,all_tasks_have_full_pass_evidence=True,\\n    member_hashes=EXPECTED_MEMBERS,zip_sha256=sha256(archive),source_bundle_sha256=sha256(WORK/'source_bundle.zip'),\\n    build_times=build_times,timings=timings,local_composite_estimate=gm,observed_new_public_score=None,\\n    fixed_case_diagnostics=diagnostics,known_cases_pass=True,universal_dqi_correctness_proven=False,\\n    chemistry_manifest_sha256=sha256(SRC/'chemistry/MANIFEST.json'),dqi_manifest_sha256=sha256(SRC/'dqi/MANIFEST.json'),\\n    verifier_sha256=EXPECTED_VERIFIERS,local_stock_host_entire_dqi_result_parity=local_host_parity,\\n    common_dqi_seed=COMMON_SEED,chemistry_seed=20261029173,salt=SALT,\\n    all_three_task_generators_complete=False,competition_submission_performed=False)\\n(WORK/'reproduction_audit.json').write_text(json.dumps(audit,indent=2))\\nprint('18-member ZIP read-back PASS. Ready for independent download audit; no competition submission performed.',flush=True)\\nshutil.rmtree(SUB);shutil.rmtree(SRC)\\n\",\"metadata\":{},\"outputs\":[],\"execution_count\":null}]}",
